{"id":"CVE-2002-2254","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2007-10-14T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-08T03:59:11.452Z","description":"The experimental IP packet queuing feature in Netfilter / IPTables in Linux kernel 2.4 up to 2.4.19 and 2.5 up to 2.5.31, when a privileged process exits and network traffic is not being queued, may allow a later process with the same Process ID (PID) to access certain network traffic that would otherwise be restricted.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://archives.neohapsis.com/archives/bugtraq/2002-12/0025.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20021203 Local Netfilter / IPTables IP Queue PID Wrap Flaw"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/6305","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"6305"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/10756","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"linux-netfilter-obtain-information(10756)"}],"vendors":["linux-kernel"]}
